  "anchors_text": "Use the full scale. Calibrate your answer against these anchor points:\n0.95-1.00 — Entirely gentle. Nothing bad happens at all. Animals play, help each other, or solve a small friendly problem. A child finishes it smiling.\n0.75-0.90 — Mild worry that resolves. A character is briefly lost, sad, or scared, but is comforted and the ending is warm and safe.\n0.55-0.70 — Real peril or injury, described without detail, fully resolved by the end. The animal recovers and is safe.\n0.35-0.50 — Something genuinely frightening or sad happens off-screen, or a threat remains unresolved at the end. Not graphic, but not comforting either.\n0.15-0.30 — Death or permanent loss happens on-screen, handled gently, but a child of this age would need an adult to talk it through.\n0.00-0.10 — Graphic violence, hunting described in physical detail, blood, or suffering shown directly. Clearly unsuitable."
